{
  "labId": "ucsd-pediatrics-lab-feldstein-lab",
  "status": "supported",
  "summaryZh": "Feldstein 实验室研究肝脏及其他器官脂肪酸和脂质过量积累所触发的细胞死亡生化通路，涉及肥胖相关肝病和二型糖尿病。方法未明确。",
  "researchQuestions": [
    "哪些过程将肝脏脂质过度积累与肝损伤、纤维化及癌变联系起来？"
  ],
  "topics": [
    "脂质与细胞死亡",
    "肥胖相关肝病",
    "二型糖尿病"
  ],
  "methods": [],
  "evidence": [
    {
      "sourceId": "src-afa663dd9d966ead",
      "quote": "Dr. Ariel Feldstein, MD Ariel Feldstein, MD investigates the biochemical pathways of cell death triggers by over-accumulation of fatty acids and other lipids in the liver and other organs, which may play an important role in disease processes such as obesity-associated liver disease (nonalcoholic steatohepatitis or NASH), and type 2 diabetes. News & Research Dr. Feldstein has been invited as a Visiting Professor to various National and International Institutions, including Universidad Catolica de Chile, Santiago, Chile (February 2012), Northwestern University (April 2012), UT Health Science Center at Houston (June 2012), Bambino Gesu Hospital, Rome, Italy (December 2012), and the University of Torino, Italy (February 2013). Spotlight Peds Focus: Gastroenterology from Rady Children's Hospital on Vimeo",
      "supports": [
        "research",
        "topics"
      ]
    },
    {
      "sourceId": "src-41ec95a3e3e8570f",
      "quote": "Feldstein Lab",
      "supports": [
        "affiliation",
        "identity"
      ]
    },
    {
      "sourceId": "src-3bb10c58f563bc1f",
      "quote": "A second objective of the lab is to better understand the events that link an excessive accumulation of lipids in the liver (steatosis) to liver injury, fibrosis and carcinogenesis.",
